\ serial.ga - node 708 takes 65536 bytes through the UART on its pins, as
\ on GreenArrays' evaluation boards, and sends back the low byte of their
\ sum: a long stream at 921600 baud, timed by unext loops as on a board.
\ On the board's inverted line a start bit is high, and data bits are low
\ for 1. Pin 17 is read in io's bit 17, and waited on through up.

node 708
: main
    io b! up a!
    0 63 for 1023 for rx + next next
    255 and send
    right a! @             \ wait forever on node 709

\ waits for the start bit, then samples the middle of each data bit, the
\ first into bit 0, and waits into the stop bit, where the line is low
: rx ( -- c )
    @ drop 214 for unext
    0 7 for
        414 for unext
        2/ @b 2/ 2/ 2/ 2/ 2/ 2/ 2/ 2/ 2/ 2/ 0x80 and 0x80 xor +
    next
    428 for unext ;

\ drives pin 1 high (3) or low (2) for a bit
: bit ( level ) !b 428 for unext ;

\ a start bit, 8 data bits from the lowest, and a stop bit, inverted
: send ( c )
    3 bit
    7 for dup 1 and 1 xor 2 + bit 2/ next drop
    2 bit ;
